ut": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T163248Z-468a0293", "fid": "R-8"}, "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "R-10 half closed: the falsified inference is restated, the two owner rulings are still open on the record", "recommendation": "Instance. The plan's first inference now reads `Disproved while building` and says what is owed, which settles that half. Both items R-10 named are still marked `Not settled by the goals` (the mid-build decisions NOTE removed with no replacement; `learnings-files --for-diff` kept without a consumer), and no ruling is recorded anywhere outside the plan (.prawduct/.handoff-notes.md and project-state.yaml carry none). A ruling is the owner's to give, so R-10 is left out of `resolutions` rather than marked fixed from the builder's edit. When the owner rules, record it outside the plan (the handoff notes or the PR body are free surfaces) and accept R-10 citing it.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T163248Z-468a0293", "fid": "R-10"}, "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "R-3 fix: the scope filter in answered_lint_results has no test, and an unscoped review is answered by every review in the shared store", "recommendation": "Instance (plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py `answered_lint_results`). Two edges of an otherwise sound fix. (1) Every test in `TestAnAnsweredRecordLintResultIsNotReRaised` writes both reviews under the fixture's one scope (`demo-scope`), so neither the scope-mismatch skip nor the `scope is None` path is exercised. With `scope=None` nothing bounds the match: a `waived` resolution of an identical `record-lint chunk-ref-missing: unchecked` result recorded by any other work in the clone-shared store demotes this review's blocker to an observation. `prior_dispositions`, which the docstring cites as the model, is bounded by cited files in that case; a chunk-level result carries no file, so here nothing is. The safer direction for the blocking half is that an unscoped review is answered by nothing. (2) A WARNING result answered by a `waived` resolution is re-raised, because `waived` fills only the `blocking` map and a warning looks up the `warning` map; that errs strict and costs a re-ask, nothing more. Neither is wrong on today's tree for a scoped review, which is what this branch is. If you fix (1), it is a judgeable edit plus a test (two reviews under different scopes; one unscoped) and buys a round, so ride a commit already planned; otherwise leave it for the boundary review.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T163248Z-468a0293", "fid": "R-3"}, "oid": "O-4"}], "duration_seconds": 900, "scope": "critic-trim", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["01", "02", "03"], "chunks_proposed": ["01", "02", "03"], "chunk": "01", "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-critic-trim.md", ".prawduct/changes/critic-trim.md", "documentation/backlog-service-cache-spec.md", "documentation/backlog-service-requirements.md", "plugin/agents/critic-reviewer.md", "plugin/skills/backlog/adapter-mode.md", "plugin/skills/backlog/cache-reads.md", "plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md", "plugin/skills/critic/cross-checks.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-protocol.md", "plugin/skills/pr/review-protocol.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01", "02", "03"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-critic-trim.md", "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-10T16:50:54Z"}}

